# Messages of the error codes of archbuilder-model (crates/archbuilder-model/src/error.rs).

ab-model-name-empty = The name cannot be empty.
ab-model-name-taken = The name "{ $name }" is already used here. Names are unique within their building, site or project, whatever the case of the letters.
ab-model-parent-invalid = "{ $name }" is not in a container of the right kind. A site belongs to the project, a building to a site, a storey or level to a building, a wall to a storey, and a door or window to a wall.
ab-model-project-not-unique = A document holds exactly one project.
ab-model-level-invalid = The storey "{ $name }" needs a level of its own that belongs to the same building and is marked as a storey level.
ab-model-wall-too-short = The wall "{ $name }" has no length. Its baseline needs two different points, at least a millimeter apart.
ab-model-level-below-walls = The level cannot go there: the top of { $count } wall(s), such as "{ $name }", would not be above its base. Move or reconnect those walls first.
ab-model-wall-top-invalid = The top of the wall "{ $name }" is not above its base. Constrain it to a higher level or give it a height.
ab-model-insert-outside = "{ $name }" does not fit in the wall "{ $wall }": the opening must lie between { $from } m and { $to } m along the wall, clear of the corners.
ab-model-insert-too-tall = "{ $name }" reaches too high in the wall "{ $wall }": the top of the opening must stay below { $top } m.
ab-model-insert-overlap = "{ $name }" overlaps "{ $other }" in the same wall. Move it or make it narrower.
ab-model-insert-operation = "{ $name }" cannot operate as { $operation }: a door swings with one or two leaves, slides, folds or pivots, and a window is fixed, casement, awning, hopper, sliding, folding or pivoting.
ab-model-insert-profile = The outline of "{ $name }" crosses itself, has no area or leaves the opening's width and height.
ab-model-insert-frame = The frame of "{ $name }" leaves no clear opening. Make the opening larger or the frame bars narrower.
ab-model-insert-meets-wall = "{ $name }" would open into the wall "{ $other }", which meets or crosses its wall there. Move it clear of that wall.
ab-model-floor-malformed = The floor "{ $name }" has no usable boundary: each loop needs at least three points inside the allowed range, and its edges must be readable.
ab-model-floor-edge-short = The floor "{ $name }" has an edge shorter than a millimeter. Move the points apart or remove one.
ab-model-floor-self-intersecting = The boundary of the floor "{ $name }" crosses or touches itself. Redraw it so that no edges cross.
ab-model-floor-area = The floor "{ $name }" has no usable area. Its outer boundary must enclose at least 1 cm² and at most 1 000 km².
ab-model-floor-hole-outside = A hole of the floor "{ $name }" is not inside its outer boundary, or touches it. Keep the hole clear of the edges.
ab-model-floor-holes-overlap = Two holes of the floor "{ $name }" overlap or lie inside each other. Keep the holes apart.
ab-model-wall-corner-open = The ends of "{ $name }" and "{ $other }" are close together but not joined: the corner is open.
ab-model-floor-edge-unsupported = An edge of the floor "{ $name }" follows the wall "{ $wall }" but runs past its ends: the wall no longer bounds the floor there.

ab-model-room-unenclosed = The room "{ $name }" ({ $number }) is not inside a closed loop of walls: it has no area until its walls close.
ab-model-room-redundant = The room "{ $name }" ({ $number }) shares its region with a room that has a lower number, which keeps the region: this one has no area until the other is removed or this one is moved.
ab-model-room-number-duplicate = The number { $number } of the room "{ $name }" is used by another room on the same storey.
ab-model-wall-overlap = "{ $name }" and "{ $other }" lie on top of each other. Rooms and floors treat them as one wall; delete one of them.
ab-model-stair-no-top = The stair "{ $name }" has no level above its base to arrive at. Add a storey above or choose a top level.
ab-model-stair-risers = The stair "{ $name }" would have { $count } risers; it needs at least { $least } and at most { $most }. Change the highest riser or the levels.
ab-model-stair-malformed = The stair "{ $name }" has a record that cannot be read.
ab-model-stair-stride = The stair "{ $name }" has a stride (twice the riser plus the tread) of { $stride } m, outside { $low }–{ $high } m: it will be uncomfortable to walk.
ab-model-stair-opening-uncut = The shaft opening of the stair "{ $name }" reaches the floor "{ $floor }" but cannot be cut out of it.
ab-model-stair-overlap = The stairs "{ $name }" and "{ $other }" overlap in plan. Move one of them.

ab-model-type-layer-count = A type has between 1 and { $most } layers; this one has { $count }. Add a layer or remove some.
ab-model-type-layer-thickness = Layer { $layer } needs a thickness above 0 and at most { $most } m. Only a membrane has no thickness.
ab-model-type-membrane-thickness = Layer { $layer } is a membrane, which has no thickness. Set its thickness to 0 or give it another function.
ab-model-type-core = The core needs at least one layer: tick the Core column of one or more layers that follow one another.
ab-model-type-total = The layers add up to { $total } mm; the total must be between { $least } mm and { $most } mm.
ab-model-type-mismatch = "{ $name }" does not match its type in { $field }. That value comes from the type: edit the type or choose another one.
ab-model-type-operation = The type "{ $name }" cannot operate as { $operation }: a door swings with one or two leaves, slides, folds or pivots, and a window is fixed, casement, awning, hopper, sliding, folding or pivoting.
ab-model-pinned = "{ $name }" is pinned. Unpin it (UP) to change it.
ab-model-roof-malformed = The roof "{ $name }" cannot be read: it needs 3 to 256 readable edges.
ab-model-roof-footprint = The footprint of the roof "{ $name }" is not a simple loop: it crosses or touches itself, or has an edge shorter than a millimeter. Redraw it or move the walls it follows.
ab-model-roof-outline = With its overhangs, the outline of the roof "{ $name }" crosses or touches itself. Make the overhangs smaller there.
ab-model-roof-no-slope = No edge of the roof "{ $name }" defines a slope. Give at least one edge a slope.
ab-model-roof-collinear-slopes = Two neighboring edges of the roof "{ $name }" lie on one line near ({ $x }, { $y }) with different slopes. Give them the same slope or remove the point between them.
ab-model-roof-unclosed = No continuous surface covers the roof "{ $name }" near ({ $x }, { $y }): that part is enclosed only by edges without slope, or an edge without slope meets an inward corner. Give that edge a slope.
ab-model-roof-degenerate = The surface of the roof "{ $name }" could not be computed reliably near ({ $x }, { $y }). Remove very short or nearly parallel edges there.
ab-model-wall-attach-failed = The wall "{ $name }" cannot follow the underside of "{ $target }": part of it is outside it, or the underside comes down to the wall's base. It keeps its own top until that changes.
ab-model-wall-attach-target = The wall "{ $name }" can attach its top only to a roof or a floor of its building.
ab-model-ceiling-malformed = The ceiling "{ $name }" has no usable boundary: each loop needs at least three points inside the allowed range, and its edges must be readable.
ab-model-ceiling-boundary = The boundary of the ceiling "{ $name }" is not usable: a loop crosses or touches itself, an edge is shorter than a millimeter, or the area is out of range. Redraw it.
ab-model-ceiling-edge-unsupported = An edge of the ceiling "{ $name }" follows the wall "{ $wall }" but runs past its ends: the wall no longer bounds the ceiling there.
ab-model-opening-footprint = The footprint of "{ $name }" is not usable: it needs at least three points, must not cross itself and must have an area.
ab-model-opening-outside-host = The opening "{ $name }" reaches outside "{ $host }", which hosts it: the part outside cuts nothing.
ab-model-floor-slope = The slope of the floor "{ $name }" is steeper than 85°. Give it a lower slope, a longer arrow or a smaller end height.
ab-model-ceiling-slope = The slope of the ceiling "{ $name }" is steeper than 85°. Give it a lower slope, a longer arrow or a smaller end height.
ab-model-ceiling-range = The underside of the ceiling "{ $name }" leaves the height of its storey: it would lie below the level or above the level over it. Move the slope arrow or lower the slope.
ab-model-ceiling-range-element = The underside of the ceiling "{ $name }" would pass through "{ $over }" above it. Lower the ceiling or the slope.

ab-model-view-range = The range of the plan view "{ $name }" is out of order: the view depth must not be above the bottom, the bottom must be below the cut height and the top above it.
ab-model-floor-edge-profile = The edge element "{ $name }" needs at least one floor edge and a profile that is a simple loop of at least three points.
ab-model-floor-edge-orphan = The edge element "{ $name }" names { $count } edge(s) that its floor no longer has. Select the edges again or delete the element.
ab-model-roof-extrusion-profile = The profile of the roof "{ $name }" needs at least two points, no segment of no length and every point within range.
ab-model-roof-extrusion-section = The thickness of the roof "{ $name }" is too large for the bends of its profile: its section would cross itself. Give it a smaller thickness or a gentler profile.
ab-model-roof-extrusion-span = The extrusion of the roof "{ $name }" must run between 10 mm and 500 m.

ab-model-ramp-no-top = The ramp "{ $name }" has no level above its base to arrive at and no rise. Add a storey above, choose a top level or give a rise.
ab-model-ramp-malformed = The ramp "{ $name }" cannot be built: a width, length, landing or thickness is not valid.
ab-model-ramp-slope = The ramp "{ $name }" has a slope of { $slope } %, over the largest of its type, { $max } %. Lengthen the run or change the type.
ab-model-railing-malformed = The railing "{ $name }" cannot be built: its path needs two different points, and a host must still exist.
ab-model-railing-gap = The railing "{ $name }" has an opening of { $gap } mm between balusters, over { $max } mm. Use a smaller baluster spacing.
ab-model-location-distant = { $count } elements lie up to { $distance } m from the internal origin, beyond the precision distance of { $limit } m, where drawing and picking lose precision. Place the model relative to the survey point (Recenter Model) or raise the precision distance.
ab-model-datum-degenerate = The datum "{ $name }" has no usable line or plane: a grid or reference plane must be at least a millimeter long and a work plane needs its datum or three points that are not on one line.
ab-model-datum-label-duplicate = The label "{ $name }" is used by { $count } grids of the building. Rename one of them.
ab-model-curtain-rule = A curtain wall type has a grid rule that cannot lay out lines: the value must be a positive number, a fixed number at most 150, an angle at most 60 degrees either way, and the two directions must not end up nearly parallel.
ab-model-curtain-panel = The system panel of a curtain wall type is glazed, solid or empty. Give a cell a door or a window as a panel of that cell.
ab-model-curtain-mullion = A curtain wall type has a mullion or panel without a usable size: the width and depth must be positive and within bounds.
ab-model-curtain-limit = The curtain wall "{ $name }" holds more grid edits or panel overrides than a wall can.
ab-model-curtain-insert = The curtain wall "{ $name }" hosts a door, window or opening. Give a cell of the wall a door or window panel instead.
ab-model-curtain-cell-shape = The removed grid segments of the curtain wall "{ $name }" leave a cell that is not a rectangle. Remove the whole segment between two cells.
ab-model-curtain-not-curtain = "{ $name }" is not a curtain wall.
ab-model-curtain-unknown = "{ $name }" is not a grid line, cell or type of this curtain wall.
